rhaps add any final points, maybe bring up Candidate A still under-discussed. According to the process, we need to still cover Candidate A before final recommendation. So Agent 1 could bring up Candidate A now, compare with C, and see if any concerns. Or could ask for more info about A's stress resilience or crew cooperation. But we need to make a public contribution referencing current discussion, stating recommendation (still Candidate C), and maybe ask a question about A. However, we must not start a new point without connecting. We can say: \"I agree with the panel's shift to Candidate C, but we still need to discuss Candidate A's stress resilience and crew cooperation before final decision.\" That would be a contribution. Also we need to include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\". Yes.\n\nThus produce:\n\nPUBLIC_MESSAGE: I agree with the panel's move to Candidate C as provisional lead... but we still need to evaluate Candidate A's stress resilience and crew cooperation, as those criteria are still open. Provide some facts about A: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. Explain that while A shows strong technical and leadership, concerns about openness to criticism and organization may affect reliability and crew cooperation. So we need to discuss.\n\nThus final."}
